# Everything here is an ARTEFACT, not source. Git must not rewrite a byte.
#
# The manifest records the SHA-256 and the exact size of every file as it left
# the publishing machine. Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM
# config, so a clone normalises CRLF to LF on the way INTO a commit - and Pages
# then serves a .cmd or a README one byte shorter per line than the manifest
# says. The updater does exactly the right thing with that:
#
#     failed on README.txt: short read: 4905 bytes, the manifest says 5027
#
# and every friend's update aborted, on every launch, for three versions.
#
# `-text` disables the conversion whatever the machine's git is set to, which
# is why it is committed here as well as set in the publishing clone.
* -text
